               "opportunityCheck":  "Exposure, market growth and position look reasonable. Vistra does sell power to hyperscalers (Meta, AWS, Microsoft solar), but most of its revenue is still general wholesale and retail power. I would lower the bottleneck and pricing-power score. Power is scarce in theory, but ERCOT prices near $30/MWh, a Texas data-center pause and regulators pushing back on who pays for data-center power all limit how much Vistra can charge. The Comanche Peak deal that hasn\u0027t been signed yet still supports the optionality score.",
               "technical":  "Trend: VST closed at $115.25 on 20 Nov 2026, below its EMA 50 ($138.25), EMA 100 ($143.50) and EMA 200 ($149.86). EMAs are smoothed average prices. With the short average under the long ones in that order, the stock is in a clear downtrend. Momentum: MACD (a trend-momentum gauge built from two EMAs) is −5.64, below its signal line at −4.71, and the histogram is −0.93. Downside momentum is still building, not fading. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 34.44, which is weak and close to oversold but not there yet. Position: price is just above the lower Bollinger Band at $113.75. The bands sit about two standard deviations either side of the 20-day average of $131.55. Price is only about 4% above the 52-week low of $110.89, and well below the 52-week high of $189.29. Volume: 8.33M shares traded on the 7.17% drop, about 26% above the 20-day average of 6.60M, and the close was near the day\u0027s low of $114.85, so sellers were in control. Support is around $110.89–113.75; resistance is the $131.55 mid-band, then the EMA 50 near $138.",
               "fundamental":  "Vistra sells AI-era electricity from a large gas and nuclear fleet. It has signed power contracts with Meta and AWS that pay for nuclear uprates, a Microsoft-contracted 405 MW Pulaski solar plant is now running, and in Q3 it signed a 20-year, 207 MW contract with New Era Energy and Digital at its Odessa gas plant in Texas. Q3 2026 net income was $1.14B, including a $559M unrealized hedge gain. Adjusted EBITDA rose to $2.38B. In October the DOE offered a conditional loan of up to $4.2B for nuclear upgrades in Pennsylvania and Ohio. The weak spots are Texas, about 40% of capacity, where prices are low and data-center policy is uncertain, and 2028, which is only 78% hedged. Pro-forma liquidity is about $5.4B after the Cogentrix purchase and the redemption of preferred shares.",
               "news":  [
                            "3–5 Nov 2026: Gina Hinojosa won the Texas governor\u0027s race on a platform that included pausing new data centers. On 4 Nov KeyBanc cut VST to Sector Weight from Overweight, and the stock fell about 13.8% to a closing low of $112.89 on 5 Nov.",
                            "6 Nov 2026: Q3 adjusted EBITDA was a record $2,378M, up from $1,581M. Vistra narrowed 2026 guidance to $7.1–7.5B and set 2027 guidance at $7.7–8.5B, and the stock jumped about 10.6% to $124.80.",
                            "6 Nov 2026: The board added $1.5B to the buyback, leaving about $2.5B to use by end-2028. Vistra also confirmed that the roughly $2.2B Cogentrix acquisition, about 5,500 MW of gas plants, closed in October.",
                            "9 Nov 2026: Vistra filed a resale prospectus for up to 5M shares held by Q-Generation Holdings, the seller in an acquisition. Vistra gets no proceeds, and the shares are locked up until 30 Jan 2027.",
                            "17 Nov 2026: BMO raised its target to $196 from $188 after cutting it on 5 Nov, and Bernstein moved its target to $182 from $181. Both kept Outperform ratings.",
                            "19–20 Nov 2026: VST fell 6.27% to $120.27, then 7.17% to $115.25, during a broad sell-off in AI-linked stocks. I found no company-specific news behind these two days."
                        ],
               "caution":  "Most of Vistra\u0027s earnings risk is now political, not operational. A new Texas governor who favors a data-center pause could slow the large-load contracts that justified the stock\u0027s 2025 rally. Low ERCOT prices hurt the roughly 22% of 2028 output that is not yet hedged. Up to 5M resale shares could come to market after 30 Jan 2027. The chart is in a full downtrend, with falling MACD and selling on above-average volume. A break below the $110.89 low would leave no recent support level.",
               "opportunity":  "The business is earning more even as the share price falls. EBITDA guidance rises from $7.1–7.5B in 2026 to $7.7–8.5B in 2027, and 2027 is about 98% hedged. Steady buybacks are shrinking the share count. Management expects adjusted free cash flow before growth per share to grow about 70% from 2027 to 2030 even without higher power prices. Signing a buyer for Comanche Peak\u0027s 1,200 MW, or more uprate deals with hyperscalers outside Texas, would lower the Texas risk. With RSI near 34 and price at the lower Bollinger Band, the stock is stretched to the downside.",
